"""
Return a monotonic nanosecond tick count for the current hosted runtime.

Sequential successful reads in one runtime instance are non-decreasing. The
origin is unspecified and is not a wall-clock or calendar timestamp. The
return value is an integer `u64`; this API performs no allocation, exposes no
platform clock structure, and does not promise one-nanosecond hardware
resolution.
"""
unsafe extern "C" verb actus_monotonic_nanos() -> u64;

"""
Read the hosted runtime's monotonic clock in nanoseconds.

The value is suitable for checked subtraction of an earlier and later read.
The runtime bridge owns platform selection and checked conversion; Actus code
does not receive a pointer, a platform-specific type, or wall-clock data.
"""
open verb monotonic_nanos() -> u64 {
    return actus_monotonic_nanos();
}
